Reader: bench/effort_replication_read.py at sha256 3a69244293ca4cd6... (stdlib only, no network). Its self-test
enumerates all 9,261 count triples, pins every threshold with literal cases one pass either side of it, and FAILS
under each of ten sabotages (every constant moved by one in each direction). Run on batch 1 it prints refusal
REPLICATES on all three lines, and order NO ROOM / REPLICATES / REPLICATES.
Reading, per cell, three lines, each stated whatever it is. A, B and C are passes per 20. A cell with any arm under
18 scored calls is NOT MEASURED (mechanical); an HTTP 400 naming a history or tool shape, or a served model other
than gpt-5.6-luna, makes the batch NOT MEASURED (read by hand from the reader's first line).
  against today's product   REPLICATES if B - A >= 5. REVERSED if A - B >= 4. Otherwise DOES NOT REPLICATE, marked
                            NO ROOM when A >= 16, so that a ceiling is never read as a contradiction.
  within the route          the same three labels on B against C.
  route effect              REPLICATES if A - C >= 3. REVERSED if C - A >= 3. Otherwise ABSENT.
  Every (A, B, C) in 0..20 maps to exactly one label on each line. There is no pooling: the second sample is read
  on its own counts, with batch 1's printed beside it.
What it decides. BUILD-CANDIDATE stands against today's product only if refusal REPLICATES on the first line. If it
DOES NOT REPLICATE there, the verdict is withdrawn to MIXED and R6 names the follow-up. A REVERSED on the first line
of either cell withdraws it as well, and a third sample of that cell comes before any design. order is expected NOT
to replicate against today's product (batch 1: +2, no room); if it does, that is reported as new information and
not as confirmation.
My estimates: refusal REPLICATES against today's product 85%, within the route 95%. Route effect REPLICATES on
order 80%, on refusal 50% (batch 1's 6 against 0, p = 0.02, is the weakest of the four comparisons).
